     My last character cleared out no less than six bones files,
leaving me with none, then died as a result of a cockatrice corpse
accident and didn't leave a bones file. So I nearly gave up the game
for ages. Just picked it up again, and decided to start another
wizard. Starting equipment included ring of poison resistance.

     In dlevel 1, I find a fountain. And quaff from it immediately (on
the grounds that if I get a bad result or get killed, I haven't wasted
much gaming time. It's after dlevel 4 that I stop quaffing from
fountains until I'm hard enough to handle water moccasins - which are
worse to deal with than the demons IMHO.) Guess what... I get a wish.

     Not sure what to wish for. I already have magic resistance from
my cloak. I could wish for decent armour, but I've always considered
that a wish wasted. Could even go for speed boots. But in the end I
wish for... Magicbane (blessed, rustproof and +2). Yes, I *know* it'll
be the first thing I get once I can get to a proper sacrifice-fest at
a co-aligned altar, but there's no guarantee that there will even BE a
coaligned altar in the game - Minetown might be cross-aligned and I
might still want the priest for donating to, and might never get a pet
hard enough to take him out so I could then convert the altar without
having to murder him myself and lose divine protection. So, magicbane
it is. Got it, blessed, rustproofed and +2. It's far better than any
armour so far.

     Dungeon level 2: There's an armour shop. Watch what pet picks up.
Try on snow boots... They're speed boots. wow.

     Read unidentified scroll. Oops, it's destroy armour - I
remembered to take off the cloak, but forgot the boots. Bye-bye speed.
But the armour shop contains *another* pair. And yippee, they're not
only speed boots but +1.

     Dungeon level 3, pet gets killed by falling rock trap. Find a
lamp. And an altar. But no monsters near the altar, and no means of
creating more monsters to sacrifice (though the only sacrifice I can
make, a nearby newt, converts it to Neutral which is my own
alignment.) The lamp turns out to be blessed...

     Dungeon level 4. General-store shop. Drop lamp to see how much it
costs. 88gp - I have a blessed magic lamp. Quaffed from fountain
again, got see invisible. I'm keeping the lamp for lighting my way in
dark Mines levels right now, but may use it for a wish later.

     Clear Sokoban (stairs are in dlevel 7, the Oracle is 6). Find bag
of holding. Tame a new housecat, which grows up to a large cat soon.
Read another unidentified scroll - unfortunately it's a scroll of
fire. Bye-bye to my spellbook of force bolt. Find new spellbook - it's
extra healing. Also a spellbook of Cure Blindness - which I cast to
increase my Healing spell abilities until I can get them to Basic.

     Get into Gnomish Mines. Reach Minetown. The altar *is* coaligned.
The large cat takes out all the watchmen and finally the watch captain
(I didn't attack any of them even once, but kept on healing my cat
while it was fighting the captain), and eats all their corpses ;-).
It's the variant of Minetown that has a spellbook store. And the first
spellbook that my cat brings me - I wasn't even trying to rob the
store at the time - is a replacement book of force bolt. *Good* kitty,
here's another tripe ration. Oh, and a gnome drops a spellbook of
fireball. All I need now to really make my day is magic missile.

     Quaffed unidentified potion. Oops, it turned out to be potion of
polymorph. Fortunately I ended up polying into a monster that could
still wear cloaks (a dwarf lord), so my cloak of magic resistance
wasn't ruined. Cat takes out two gray unicorns. Eat one, get poison
resistance. Let the cat eat the other. Remember not to sacrifice
either, but keep one of their horns. Also have sleep and cold
resistance by now (eating elves and yetis).

     The only bit of bad luck is that Izchak's shop is infested with
mimics and contains only four genuine candles. Will have to consider
spending a wish on them later if I don't find three others in the
game. This is the first time I've seen Izchak have less than seven
candles. I consider killing him in revenge but decide against it.

     Unfortunately, am now level 11 and can't afford the first bit of
the protection racket. May have to off a shopkeeper to get the cash to
do that, but am not yet sure I'm hard enough to take one on yet. May
try for the luckstone first, assuming there is one.

